<title>HUNGARY: Hungary household savings up HUF 40.9 bln in Feb.</title>
<headline>Hungary household savings up HUF 40.9 bln in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's net household savings rose 40.9 billion forints in January to 2,506.7 billion forints ($14.18 billion), the National Bank of Hungary said on Friday.</p>
<p> (in billion forints)    Feb '97    Jan '97	Feb' 96</p>
<p> Forint savings	    2,359.5    2,318.9	1,825.3</p>
<p> Foreign currency	    479.0	478.7	  452.1</p>
<p> Total savings	     2,838.5    2,797.6	2,277.4</p>
<p> Total loans		   331.8	331.8	  361.5</p>
<p> Net household savings   2,506.7    2,465.8	 1,915.9</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures are not inflation-adjusted. February 1997 figures are preliminary. Consumer price inflation was 18.8 percent year-on-year in February.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4042</p>
